From: lgautier at gmail.com (Laurent Gautier)
Date: Fri, 07 Oct 2011 23:03:29 +0200
Subject: Re: [Rpy] How to specify na_rm=True?
In-Reply-To: <4E8C4D07.9090106@cornell.edu>
References: <4E8C4D07.9090106@cornell.edu>
Message-ID: <4E8F6921.7040509@gmail.com>

This is happening because the signature of the R function is:
base::mean(x, ...)

No na.rm in sight, therefore no na_rm by default on the Python side - 
see http://rpy.sourceforge.net/rpy2/doc-dev/html/robjects_functions.html

r['mean_default'](data_NA, na_rm=True)

or

r.mean(data_NA, **{'na.rm': True})

should work.


L.

